======================================================================================================================
REFIT CHECK -- the cached held-out predictions must come back identical
======================================================================================================================
  Only held-out predictions were persisted and CQR needs the
  calibration block, so QTREE is refitted. Everything feeding it is
  deterministic, so the refit must reproduce the cache exactly.

  THE CACHE HOLDS PREDICTIONS AFTER BOTH ENFORCEMENT PASSES -- quantile
  axis, then horizon axis -- so the refit gets the same two passes,
  across all five horizons of each group, BEFORE it is compared. An
  earlier version applied only the quantile pass. Horizon enforcement
  had moved 0.16-0.68% of QTREE's predictions in every group, so that
  version would have aborted on every run, blaming a drift that never
  happened and advising deletion of a cache that was correct.

  cache fingerprint matches (9e332d92a2945b03...).

