======================================================================================================================
THE CORRECTION -- one set of widths per cell, fitted on val only
======================================================================================================================
  A NEGATIVE width is legitimate: it means the raw interval was too
  wide on val and conformalisation TIGHTENS it. The outer pair targets
  90% coverage and the inner pair 50%.
  q-reorder: CQR widens each pair independently, which can cross the
  levels. h-reorder: each horizon has its own widths, which can break
  the running max in k, so it is re-applied -- every other model in the
  table is horizon-enforced and this one must be too. The horizon pass
  only RAISES predictions, so it can erode a pair's guarantee slightly
  at its lower bound; the rate says by how much it touched.

