======================================================================================================================
WHAT IS AND IS NOT DEMONSTRATED
======================================================================================================================
  NOT TESTED: CQR's guarantee. The interval-coverage table carries no
  intervals and sits within ~1pp of nominal before any correction, so
  it cannot say whether the guarantee holds on either half.
  DEMONSTRATED, where the counts above say so: a correction fitted on
  val shrinks the 5-level calibration gap, by paired intervals that
  exclude zero, against the ~1 per half chance would produce. The
  isotonic recalibration managed 0 of 80 on the same kind of test.
  THE MECHANISM is whatever the per-level breakdown shows -- location
  (q50) or tightening (the pair levels) -- and is not asserted beyond it.
  Levels here are a later look at rows already scored; the raw-versus-
  CQR differences are within-row contrasts and are the new measurement.
======================================================================================================================
